---
description: "Enterprise Grade Rules for Chrome Extension (React 18, JS/TS, Web3, Webpack)"
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Role
Senior Frontend Engineer specializing in Chrome Extension, React, TypeScript, Web3, and Webpack build optimization.

# Core Principles
- Clean, maintainable, production-ready, secure code
- Early return, reduce nested logic
- DRY, modular, single-responsibility components
- Minimal changes, no side effects
- Type safety and strict code quality
- Extension security & performance first

# JavaScript & TypeScript Rules
- Strict TypeScript; avoid any; clear type definitions
- Consistent code style between JS and TS
- Explicit function parameters and return types
- Handle null / undefined safely
- Reuse types and utilities
- No implicit global variables
- Avoid deprecated APIs

# React 18 Rules
- Functional components only
- Follow React Hooks rules strictly
- Optimize re-renders with useMemo / useCallback
- Clean up effects in useEffect
- Event handlers start with "handle"
- Remove unused imports and variables
- Stable component structure

# Chrome Extension Rules
- Follow Chrome Extension MV3 / MV2 best practices
- Use chrome API safely with try/catch
- Isolate content scripts, background, popup logic
- No sensitive logic exposed to frontend
- Storage access with proper error handling
- Permission-safe code
- Avoid memory leaks in long-running background
- Message passing standardized and typed

# Web3 / Crypto Rules
- Use eth-sig-util, ethereumjs-util safely
- Secure key and signature handling
- No private key exposure
- Validate all inputs and signatures
- Handle wallet and encryption errors
- Use buffer and crypto-browserify properly
- Strict encoding/hex/bytes validation

# DOM & Parsing Rules
- Use cheerio, xmldom, xpath safely
- Avoid XSS risks in DOM parsing
- Sanitize HTML and third-party content
- Handle invalid XML/HTML gracefully

# Utility Rules
- Use uuid, jsonpath, path-browserify properly
- Reusable utility functions
- Consistent error handling
- Avoid redundant polyfills

# Styling (SCSS/CSS)
- Scoped styles for extension UI
- Clean, maintainable structure
- No global style pollution
- Consistent spacing, colors, layout

# Webpack & Build Rules
- Optimize bundle size
- Avoid duplicate dependencies
- Use browser polyfills properly
- Stable plugin usage
- Production build optimization

# Error Handling
- Try/catch for async and chrome API
- No silent failures
- Clear error logs
- Fallback UI for critical errors

# Comments & TODO Standards
- JSDoc for public and complex functions
- Explain intent, not syntax
- Remove debug & dead comments

- TODO(Bug): Known bugs, edge cases, runtime issues
- TODO(Unfinished): Incomplete logic
- TODO(Optimize): Refactor, performance, cleanup

# Code Review Focus
- Logic bugs, null/undefined errors
- Unused code, redundancy
- Type issues, missing types
- React Hook dependency issues
- Chrome API misuse
- Extension security risks
- Web3 signature & validation issues
- Potential XSS vulnerability
- Boundary abnormal processing
- Performance & bundle size